@$VER: AmiGameBoy.guide 1.0.1 (13.11.2026)

@node MAIN "AmiGameBoy"
AmiGameBoy 1.0 is a community version for AGA Amigas.
It emulates the original mono Game Boy.

Choose a section:
@{"What it is" link ABOUT}
@{"Requirements" link REQUIREMENTS}
@{"Starting a game" link START}
@{"Controls" link CONTROLS}
@{"Battery saves" link SAVES}
@{"The menu" link MENU}
@{"Not supported" link NOTSUPPORTED}
@{"Known issues" link ISSUES}
@{"Credits" link CREDITS}
@{"Licence and source" link LICENCE}
@{"History" link HISTORY}
@endnode

@node ABOUT "What it is"
AmiGameBoy is an emulator for original mono Game Boy games.
It runs .gb cartridges on AGA Amigas and provides sound,
battery saves and a CD32 pad.

While a game runs, the program takes over the Amiga and
drives the AGA chips directly.

@{"Main menu" link MAIN}
@endnode

@node REQUIREMENTS "Requirements"
- An AGA Amiga, such as an A1200 or A4000, or an AGA FPGA
  core, with AmigaOS 3.0 or later.
- A 68020 or better. A 68030 at 50 MHz or faster is
  recommended for full speed.
- About twice the cartridge size plus 256 KB of memory.
  Fast RAM is preferred. A 1 MB cartridge needs about
  2.3 MB free.
- asl.library, supplied with AmigaOS.

@{"Main menu" link MAIN}
@endnode

@node START "Starting a game"
There is one program: AGA. It suits an A1200 with a
68030/50 and faster machines.

Workbench: start AGA. Choose Insert in the menu, select
a cartridge, then choose Power ON. The requester lists
drawers and .gb / .gbc files. Change its pattern to show
other names.

Shell: enter `AGA game.gb`

Project icons: give a cartridge an icon with AGA as its
default tool and set the tool path. Double-click the icon
to start the game.

Esc returns to the menu. Choose Continue to resume.
No games are included; use cartridge images you may
legally have.

@{"Main menu" link MAIN}
@endnode

@node CONTROLS "Controls"
Keyboard (always active):
  Cursor keys                Up, Down, Left, Right
  Left Amiga or Left Shift   A
  Left Alt or Space          B
  Del                        Select
  Help                       Start
  Esc                        Return to the menu

Joystick in port 2: fire is A; second fire is B. Use the
keyboard for the other buttons.

CD32 pad in port 2:
  Red      A
  Blue     B
  Green    B
  Yellow   Select
  Play     Start
  Hold A shoulder button with Play to return to the menu.

The program writes AmiGameBoy.config beside itself on
first start. Set one button per line, for example:
  Green = Start

Buttons: Red, Blue, Green, Yellow, L, R, Play.
Choices: A, B, Select, Start, Up, Down, Left, Right,
Nothing. The file is read at startup. Delete it to restore
the defaults. The menu Help page shows the original pad
layout; the list above shows the active defaults.

@{"Main menu" link MAIN}
@endnode

@node SAVES "Battery saves"
Games that save keep battery RAM in a .sav file beside
the cartridge. The save has the same name, for example
Game.gb and Game.sav. The file is loaded when the
cartridge is inserted.

If a save has changed, the program asks before writing it
when you insert another cartridge or quit. To keep a save,
press Esc to return to the menu, choose Quit or Insert,
then answer Save. Do not switch off or reset from inside
a game.

@{"Main menu" link MAIN}
@endnode

@node MENU "The menu"
LCD fade chooses the screen palette: Grey, Green, Blue
or Red.

Save Prefs writes settings to S:AmiGameBoy.prefs.

@{"Main menu" link MAIN}
@endnode

@node NOTSUPPORTED "Not supported"
- Game Boy Color-only cartridges are refused with a
  message. Dual-mode cartridges run in mono.
- The link cable.
- Super Game Boy features, including borders and
  palettes.
- Frozen games (snapshots), cheats, the monitor, and the
  joystick type setting from the original menu. Keyboard,
  joystick and CD32 pad are always active.

Cartridge types MBC1, MBC2, MBC3 and MBC5 up to 2 MB
are handled.

@{"Main menu" link MAIN}
@endnode

@node ISSUES "Known issues"
- Infinity hangs before its title.
- Last Crown Warriors has a grey background on story
  pages. This is cosmetic.
- Chantey has a white band in the intro. This is cosmetic.
- Final Fantasy Legend II and Mega Man V run slower on a
  68030/50.
- Cartridges with a 128 KB save, such as Last Crown
  Warriors, are untested.

@{"Main menu" link MAIN}
@endnode

@node CREDITS "Credits"
Juan Antonio Gómez Gálvez: AmiGameBoy, the menu and the
display.

Ville Helin and Ventzislav Tzvetkov: Wzonka-Lad and its
Game Boy engine.

Multivac: icons and graphics in Juan's original.

z00p: the community version and sound.

@{"Main menu" link MAIN}
@endnode

@node LICENCE "Licence and source"
AmiGameBoy is free software under the GNU General Public
License, version 2. See COPYING. It comes with no
warranty. Juan's code is used and relicensed with his
consent. Wzonka-Lad is also GPL-2.

The CD32 pad reader, cd32pad.s, is under the MIT licence.
See cd32pad.LICENSE in the source.

The source is included with the release.

@{"Main menu" link MAIN}
@endnode

@node HISTORY "History"
Juan began AmiGameBoy in 1996-97; his last public version,
0.96, is available on Aminet. In 2026 he sent his sources
to the community. Version 1.0 keeps his menu and AGA
display and uses Wzonka-Lad's engine for timing, memory
controllers, battery saves and four-channel sound.

@{"Main menu" link MAIN}
@endnode
